      "hierarchy": "supporting",
      "style": "midway",
      "narrative": "The Midway's pleasure garden: a thirteen-wide walk from the east avenue to the helter skelter's forecourt, with a kerbed parterre either side of it under a clipped hedge - moss, blocks of wool and flowers between them - a specimen tree at the centre of each bed, benches on the verges, and four striped pergolas over the walk for the only vertical rhythm in it. The outer shoulders are left informal, where the ground layer's own wildflowers are. No building anywhere in it, and nothing that pretends to be a machine.\n"
